  "final_message": "I will wait for the file listing to complete.\nI have launched the listing command and will wait for the background task to complete.\nI have launched the listing command and will wait for it to finish.\nI am waiting for `npm test` to finish.\nI will wait for the background tasks to finish.\nI will wait for the arch and listing tasks to finish.\nI am checking git history and status.\nI will wait for the task to finish.\nI am checking the directory.\nI will wait for the task to finish.\nI will wait for the directory listing of agents-vs-gates.\nI will wait for the task to complete.\nI will wait for the directory listing.\nI will wait for the task to finish.\nI will wait for the task listing.\nI will wait for the task to finish.\nI will wait for the directory listing.\nI will wait for the task to finish.\nI will wait for the directory listing.\nI will wait for the task to finish.\nI am waiting for `npm test` to finish.\nI will wait for the test task to finish.\nI am waiting for `typecheck` and `arch` checks to finish.\nI will wait for the typecheck and arch checks to finish.\nI am checking git status and diff.\nI will wait for the git status task to finish.\n`channel` cannot be safely removed from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) yet. \n\n### Downstream Consumer Dependency\nWhile `orders-service` does not internally depend on `channel`, checking downstream consumer services reveals that [`analytics-ingest`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L25-L46) relies on `channel` from the `orders.placed` event:\n- [`decodeOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L25-L46) validates that `channel` is present and one of `\"web\" | \"store\" | \"marketplace\"`.\n- Missing `channel` triggers a `ContractViolationError`, causing ingestion to fail and preventing orders from being written to the `orders` lake table ([`OrderRow.channel`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/rows.ts#L4-L12)).\n\n### Deprecation Actions Taken\nTo avoid breaking deployed consumers while marking the field for sunset (per the event versioning and deprecation guidelines):\n1. **Preserved and deprecated on event**: Marked `channel` as `@deprecated` on [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L16-L20) in [events.ts](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts).\n2. **Marked deprecated on model**: Annotated `channel` as `@deprecated` on [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/orders-service/src/core/order.ts#L16-L30) and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/orders-service/src/core/order.ts#L32-L43) in [order.ts](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/orders-service/src/core/order.ts).\n3. Complete removal can proceed once the Data team updates `analytics-ingest` to no longer require `channel`.\n\nAll builds, unit tests (`npm test`), type checks (`npm run typecheck`), and architecture checks (`npm run arch`) continue to pass.\n",
